# Vault index for Claude

This file is imported by `~/.claude/CLAUDE.md`, so it is in context in every session. It lists the
projects kept in this vault, and says where new skills and agents go.

## In every session

- Answer in short, plain English. Lead with the answer. The user, or their own instructions, may
  say otherwise.
- Create a new personal skill or agent in this vault, not straight in `~/.claude/skills` or
  `~/.claude/agents`, unless the user names another place. The vault is
  `~/.claude/second-brain-vault/`: `claude/` there for any project, `<Path>/claude/` for one below.
  Then run `second-brain link --apply`, or Claude Code never loads it (steps: `claude/README.md`).
- A rule about one project goes under `## Rules` in `<Path>/claude/README.md`, or its subproject's
  note; only a rule for every project goes in `~/.claude/CLAUDE.md`. Unsure which: ask.
- Plugin skills: `story-tracker` writes ticket text and tracks tasks, `sprint` runs a sprint,
  `vault-setup` sets up the vault or a project, `vault-doctor` checks them.
  Plugin agents: `scrum-master` for the sprint cadence,
  `docs-keeper` for docs that follow the code and for a ticket marked done.
- Write a pull request description in the format of
  `~/.claude/second-brain-vault/claude/pull-request.md`; a project's own
  `<Path>/claude/pull-request.md` wins.

## Working on a project or on notes

A request that touches no project below and no note in this vault needs nothing from the rest of
this file.

- When a request belongs to a project below, read `<Path>/README.md`, then
  `<Path>/claude/README.md` (its rules, skills, agents) and
  the `claude/subprojects/<name>.md` that `second-brain context` names, before anything else.
- Before reading or writing notes, run `second-brain conventions` and follow it. The full note is
  `~/.claude/second-brain-vault/obsidian-conventions.md`.

## Rules for notes that most often go wrong

- Find and read notes with the helper, never with grep, cat or sed on vault files:
  `second-brain find`, `search` (also for related notes before a decision), `task head`, then
  `outline` and a ranged read, and a whole note last.
- A task note is always `<project>/tasks/<TICKET-ID>/README.md`. Never file it inside the topic
  it is about; tie it to the topic with a tag that is the folder path, lowercased.
- A bare `[[Alias]]` does not resolve. Links carry a path:
  `[[<vault path or unique file name>|<alias>]]`.
- Move and rename notes with the helper (`second-brain move`, `second-brain rename`), never `mv`.
- Frontmatter is the truth. Read a status from the `status` property, never from prose.
- Ticket text is never written freehand. Use `story-tracker`: it opens with `*As a* <persona>,` /
  `*I need to* ...,` / `*so that* ...` and holds at most 4 acceptance criteria.

